  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Right to freedom of association and collective bargaining legislation in line with C87/C98</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">T&#xfc;rkiye is a member of the ILO since 18.07.1937 and has ratified 59 ILO Conventions including all fundamental conventions and 3 out of 4 governance conventions and 46 technical conventions. Out of the 59 Conventions ratified by T&#xfc;rkiye, 53 are in force, 2 Conventions have been denounced, 3 instruments abrogated. The most recent ratifications by T&#xfc;rkiye were on 23 March 2015 with C167- Safety and Health in Construction Convention and C176- Safety and Health in Mines Convention. ILO is supporting the Turkish constituents in relation to better implementation of ratified conventions, especially the fundamental conventions. The ILO also supports the constituents in reporting obligations to ensure quality reports. ILO takes an active role both within the evaluation as well as the design process of the new UNSDCF.</narrative>
  </description>
